Z||000010||Tigger||08-29-2001||09:22 AM||||Even if it happened to be an '84, doesn't mean it couldn't be a GREAT car.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>For the interior lights not turning off I'd look at the door ajar switches up by the hinges.  For the windows, if they are pwr windows put a voltmeter at the plug to check for a break in the line.  Good luck, fixing and restoring any car takes patience.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue4.gif">   <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/tatooine/spielberg/241/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||12
